{
  "summary": "The experiment tested a baseline multimodal configuration combining PCA-encoded RNA data and ResNet50-encoded images via concatenation fusion, without aggregation. Validation accuracy of 0.5266 and F1 of 0.5104 suggest multimodal fusion may provide some value compared to single-modality baselines, though no direct comparison was made. The role of specific encoders or fusion method in performance remains uncertain without additional comparative experiments."
}

